/* ML shelf, Part 5, Lesson 27: PyTorch Lightning with the agent. Follows HW10's fit_classifier and run_epoch (the loop this lesson hands to the Trainer), the setup cells of HW6, HW8, HW9 and HW10 (seed_everything, seeded loader generators), the checkpoint habits of HW6 1.4 and HW8 2C, and the project brief (project.pdf: PyTorch Lightning recommended, well-commented code worth 80 percent). Andrew Ng's Deep Learning Specialization course 2 (an efficient iteration loop, train, dev and test sets, early stopping) and course 3 (orthogonalization, one number to compare runs) are the spine, with the Lightning 2.6 documentation (LightningModule, LightningDataModule, Trainer flags, hooks, logging, ModelCheckpoint, EarlyStopping, CSVLogger) for the mechanics. The lesson data are fresh: 600 points in three Gaussian blobs from default_rng(2727) with 8 percent of labels redrawn, split 400, 100, 100 by the same generator, standardized with training statistics. Every number, hook order, file listing and message was produced with PyTorch 2.15 and Lightning 2.6.6 on the CPU of this build. */
